    "body": "## PR Summary\n\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\n**High Risk**\nChanges KV cache layout and the hot software-attention path for 128-dim heads when the option is on; incorrect indexing or copy logic could corrupt attention or staging, though default builds remain row-major.\n\n**Overview**\nAdds optional **VNNI-packed K storage** for 128-dimension attention heads behind the new CMake flag `TRON_K_VNNI` (default **OFF**). When enabled, `kv_block` holds K in `k_vnni_tensor` instead of row-major bf16; typed APIs (`store_row` / `load_row`, `page::set_k_row` / `get_k_row` / `k_packed`) replace direct row views for those slots.\n\n**Attention and writes:** `save_k` scatters rows into the packed layout; software attention scores VNNI pages with the new AVX-512 reader `k_vnni::qk_group` instead of the dotter loop. Dense AMX QK is **disabled** for VNNI slots until a matching AMX kernel lands. FPGA/GOF staging uses an updated `page_info::k_head_fn(slot, head, scratch)` that materializes a contiguous row when needed.\n\n**CI/tests:** Legacy CMake workflow and docs build with `-DTRON_K_VNNI=ON` alongside AMX dispatch; adds `t_k_vnni_layout` and broad `t_llama_unit` / integration updates (wider split-join tolerances when VNNI is on).\n\n<sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit a5697f86d318e6a87badd4a751a005da52a9c25c. Bugbot is set up for automated code reviews on this repo. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->",
